  3. Implement chart-first layout, compact query toolbar, row controls, freshness/status, local viewport operations, and typed remote action callbacks.
  4. Add focused F# tests and F# Playwright verifier covering desktop/mobile geometry and representative operations.
  5. Update TAResearch WBS/Test/Verification/DevLog and package README.
- Read/modify scope: `src/PulseTrade.Comm.Spa.Dynamic.Renderer`, corresponding tests/verifier, and `doc/TAResearch` current-state documents.
- Acceptance: Release builds pass; focused tests pass; browser verifier confirms nonblank chart, no incoherent overlap, usable desktop/mobile controls, local-only view operations, and typed remote action emission.
- Risks: WebSharper metadata compatibility of the transport-neutral contracts assembly; stale `wsfscservice`; generated bundle churn.
- Prompt summary: Continue according to WBS order, implement PTMD/Dynamic before PTCS.Host, and require thoughtful Playwright UI verification.

